  "body": "Bring the family together, entertain with ease and enjoy the best of coastal living. Set in sought-after Torbay, this versatile four-bedroom home offers sea views, multiple living spaces and a flexible layout designed to suit modern family life.\r\n\r\nThe heart of the home is the spacious open-plan living and dining area, seamlessly connected to a well-appointed kitchen. Whether it's busy weekday mornings, family dinners or weekends spent entertaining friends, this welcoming space makes everyday living easy.\r\n\r\nStep out onto the balcony and enjoy the coastal outlook, or head to the separate deck for a quiet morning coffee, a good book or relaxed evenings outdoors. With multiple outdoor spaces and room to spread out, everyone can find their own favourite spot.\r\n\r\nFour bedrooms provide flexibility for growing families, visiting guests or those needing extra room to work from home. The ground-floor bedrooms offer practical options for family members or guests, while the upper-level bedroom provides additional privacy. The multi-level layout creates a natural separation between shared living areas and private retreats.\r\n\r\nA separate laundry and internal-access garage add everyday convenience, while the versatile layout gives you plenty of options to make the home your own.\r\n\r\nBeyond the front door, enjoy the lifestyle that makes Torbay so desirable. Torbay Village offers local cafés and shops, while Waiake Beach and Long Bay are perfect for swimming, coastal walks and relaxed seaside afternoons. Browns Bay provides further shopping and dining options, with Albany's major retail centres also within easy reach.\r\n\r\nWhether you're looking for more room for the family, space to welcome guests or a home with flexible living options, this Torbay property is well worth your attention.\r\n\r\nContact us today to arrange your viewing or join us at the next open home!\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: All photos are sourced from Lot 2 and are for marketing purposes only. Layouts, features and finishes may vary between lots. Buyers are advised to make their own enquiries to confirm the details of the specific property.",
